        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> adamrk created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15145#discussion_r4470167993\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Note: I'm a bit worried that sticking this tag in the <code>HostResourceIndex</code> could cause problems later since we don't have anything in the type system indicating that the tags exist. It seems to be worth about 1.5% of the overall 5% improvement in the http proxy benchmark, so I'm not really sure if it's worth it. I also tried just using a separate bool, but that seems to be a wash overall.</p>\n<p>So I think we could remove the take and loose the fastest <code>Elided</code> path altogether, or maybe if we think index tagging could be useful in general it might make sense to introduce it into the types and use it here.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 637560181,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793809361
    },
